          "date": "2026-11-03 23:26:36.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lmv: create subdirectories on pool MDTs",
        "message": "LU-21061 lmv: create subdirectories on pool MDTs\n\nA client chooses the MDT of a new directory without looking at the\npool of the mkdir layout or of the parent default LMV, so a tree that\nis limited to a pool still gets subdirectories on any MDT.\n\nHave lmv_locate_tgt_create() get that pool, with a reference, from\nlmv_pool_mdts() and pass it to the QoS, round-robin and space\nbalanced choices.  Do not fall back to the parent MDT when it is not\nin the pool, but to any active MDT of the pool, since QoS and\nround-robin skip the MDTs that connected less than qos_maxage/2 ago,\nand fail with -ENOSPC when no MDT of the pool can be used.  Keep the\nEDQUOT retries in the pool too.  The QoS and round-robin choices lock\nthe pool before their own locks, as LOD does, and check it with the\nnew lu_tgt_check_index_locked().\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I82b08304e911f51e2d0b96d73b9e16c90d3cf3b6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
